# QuorumForge deliberation — normalization showcase
# --------------------------------------------------
# The three claims below are phrased differently but normalize to the same
# proposition. Run `quorumforge inspect samples/normalization.qf` to see the
# `normalized` field collapse the hedges and contractions.

delib | normalization | Does the release candidate meet the latency budget?

agent | q1 | Quill  | 1.0 | qa
agent | q2 | Rho    | 1.2 | perf
agent | q3 | Sable  | 0.9 | product

# These normalize identically: "the p99 latency is under 200ms"
claim | n1 | latency | I think the p99 latency is under 200ms.
claim | n2 | latency | The p99 latency is under 200ms!
claim | n3 | latency | Arguably, the p99 latency is under 200ms.

# A distinct claim with a contraction that expands during normalization.
claim | n4 | latency | The service isn't dropping requests under load.

pos | q1 | n1 | support    | 0.8 | measured 180ms in staging
